# Frontend environment variables (safe to commit - contains no secrets)
#
# VITE_API_URL = public origin of the backend API, WITHOUT the /api suffix.
# Leave it empty when the frontend and API are served from the same origin
# (local Vite dev proxy, or the Node server serving dist/).
#
# Example for a separately hosted frontend:
# VITE_API_URL=https://your-api-host.example.com
VITE_API_URL=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Backend environment variables go in server/.env, which is git-ignored.
# Do NOT put any of these here: this file is committed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# There is no JWT_SECRET any more. Sessions are opaque random identifiers held
# in the database, so there is no signing key to keep, rotate or leak.
#
# SESSION_IDLE_MINUTES   sign-out after this long without activity, default 30
# SESSION_ABSOLUTE_HOURS sign-out after this long no matter how active,
#                        default 8. This is the hard ceiling.
# SESSION_MAX_PER_USER   simultaneous sessions per staff account, default 3.
#                        Signing in beyond the limit closes the oldest ones.
# SESSION_COOKIE_SECURE  true when the browser reaches the API over HTTPS.
#                        Defaults to on when NODE_ENV=production. Turn it off
#                        only for local http development.
# SESSION_COOKIE_SAMESITE  strict | lax | none, default strict. Only change
#                        this if the frontend and API are on different sites,
#                        and read SESSIONS.md first: 'none' requires a real
#                        CSRF token, not just this value.
# DB_HOST / DB_PORT / DB_USER / DB_PASSWORD / DB_NAME
# SEED_ADMIN_PASSWORD   used only when the users table is empty. Create the
#                       remaining roles from Settings > Staff after first login.
# CORS_ORIGINS          comma-separated list of allowed browser origins, e.g.
#                       https://your-frontend.vercel.app. When empty, any origin
#                       is accepted, which is only appropriate for local dev.
# TRUST_PROXY_HOPS      number of reverse proxies in front of the app, default 1.
#                       Set this so client IPs in rate limiting are accurate.
# PORT                  default 4000
